-The immutable v\paperversion\ release has the following canonical structure:
-\begin{lstlisting}
-Projector_Resolved_Seed_Calculus_I_v1.2.1/
-  README.md
-  CHANGELOG.md
-  RELEASE.json
-  REPRODUCIBILITY.md
-  CITATION.cff
-  CITATION.bib
-  LICENSE_STATUS.md
-  MANIFEST.md
-  SHA256SUMS.txt
-  Run_All.ps1
-  Run_All.sh
-  paper/
-    Projector_Resolved_Seed_Calculus_I.tex
-    Projector_Resolved_Seed_Calculus_I.pdf
-    figures/
-  code/python/
-    seed_calculus/
-    tests/
-    pyproject.toml
-    requirements.in
-    requirements.lock.txt
-    run_all.py
-    dist/
-  formalization/lean/
-  results/
-  provenance/
-\end{lstlisting}
-
-The top-level \texttt{Run\_All.ps1} and \texttt{Run\_All.sh} copy the release to a temporary directory, reproduce the Python results and figures, execute the tests, rebuild and smoke-test the wheel, run the warning-fatal Lean build, theorem-map checker, and fail-closed kernel audit, and recompile the paper. The canonical extracted release is not modified. Exact tool versions, random seeds, tolerances, commands, and result classifications are recorded in \texttt{REPRODUCIBILITY.md} and \texttt{results/run\_record.json}. The sorted checksum manifest covers the release members but excludes itself; the archive has a separate external SHA-256 sidecar.
-
-The file \texttt{provenance/Paper\_I\_Audit\_Ledger\_v0.1.0.md} is preserved as a historical audit of v1.0.0. Current completion artifacts in the same directory describe v1.2.1 and do not rewrite that historical record.
